+    /*
+     * This is a SH8601 QSPI panel (SPI transactions), not an RGB LCD.
+     * The RGB LVGL adapter flushes immediately after draw_bitmap returns,
+     * although SPI pixel transfers are still queued for DMA. That lets LVGL
+     * overwrite the draw buffer while the LCD still reads it (horizontal
+     * corruption) and can create unbounded SPI transaction recycling stalls.
+     *
+     * The SPI adapter registers on_color_trans_done on io_handle and
+     * acknowledges LVGL flush only from the SPI completion callback.
+     * Keep the existing small internal DMA buffer and conservative QSPI
+     * settings unchanged until this independent sync fix is validated.
